C 2+2W
"Two threads each write to both locations and then read the OTHER thread's write
 to the location it wrote second.  Reading a=b=1 forces mo to run against program
 order on both locations -- W(y,2) mo W(y,1) and W(x,2) mo W(x,1) -- closing a
 cycle in (hb u mo):  W(x,1) -po-> W(y,2) -mo-> W(y,1) -po-> W(x,2) -mo-> W(x,1).
 SRA's strong-write-coherence forbids that cycle.  RA's write-coherence only
 forbids mo;hb, and neither mo step is followed by hb back to its source, so RA
 ALLOWS the outcome.  This is the separating behaviour of Lahav et al., POPL 2016,
 tabulated as Ex. 3.6 in Lahav & Boker, TOPLAS 2022."
{ }
P0 (atomic_int* x, atomic_int* y) {
  atomic_store_explicit(x,1,memory_order_release);
  atomic_store_explicit(y,2,memory_order_release);
  int r0 = atomic_load_explicit(y,memory_order_acquire);
}
P1 (atomic_int* x, atomic_int* y) {
  atomic_store_explicit(y,1,memory_order_release);
  atomic_store_explicit(x,2,memory_order_release);
  int r1 = atomic_load_explicit(x,memory_order_acquire);
}
exists (0:r0=1 /\ 1:r1=1)
